Third-party software
--------------------

Go modules compiled into gusto and gusto-helper (checked 13 October 2026 by reading each module's licence file):
  18 Apache-2.0, 4 BSD-3-Clause, 1 BSD-2-Clause, 3 MIT. None is GPL, LGPL, AGPL or MPL.
  `go list -deps ./cmd/gusto ./cmd/gusto-helper` lists them.

The usage index (internal/usage) adds a pure Go database driver for each of SQLite and Postgres, so that the release
builds with CGO_ENABLED=0 (checked 19 October 2026 by reading each module's licence file). None is GPL, LGPL, AGPL or MPL:
  modernc.org/sqlite, modernc.org/libc, modernc.org/mathutil, modernc.org/memory
                  BSD-3-Clause (the SQLite code it carries is in the public domain; its sqlite-vec extension, MIT,
                  is not imported)
  github.com/jackc/pgx/v5, pgpassfile, pgservicefile, puddle/v2
                  MIT
  github.com/dustin/go-humanize, mattn/go-isatty, ncruces/go-strftime
                  MIT
  github.com/google/uuid, remyoudompheng/bigfft, golang.org/x/sync
                  BSD-3-Clause

The design tokens (tokens.css) and the mark (mark.png) in internal/web/static are Latentic's own.

Files served from the binary (internal/web/static, see PROVENANCE.md there):
  htmx            BSD-style (htmx.org)
  highlight.js    BSD 3-Clause
  Sora (font)     SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Lucide (icons)  ISC

Programs a person may install beside gusto, which gusto runs and does not link:
  OpenShell       Apache-2.0 (github.com/NVIDIA/OpenShell)
  e2fsprogs       mke2fs, debugfs and e2fsck are GPL version 2. The release carries them as separate programs with their
                  licence and the source address, built by deploy/e2fsprogs/build.sh.
